WEBVTT

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.290
I don't like this.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:40.250
It is especially problematic
that you attacked the others.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.870
What if you started fighting
and someone's face was injured?

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.750
Are you not future actors?

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.450
You will turn in a written apology
and do one week of school clean up.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.620
As it is, if you are aiming to
enter the musical department,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.330
then please be sure to restore
your honor at the debut performance.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.040
The punishment wasn't as bad as I expected.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.250
I thought we'd be suspended.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.080
I heard from Toraishi

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.410
that Hiragi is the one who
negotiated with the teachers for us.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.540
Hiragi did?

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.330
He seems uncaring, but he
might actually be a kind person.

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:32.450
Jeez, whose fault was it that we got in trouble?

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.950
More importantly,
if we don't hurry, we'll be late.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.040
What do you mean, "more importantly"?!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.160
Crap, practice is about to start!

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.660
Run, everyone! Run!

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.250
You know what--

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.580
"Newcomers' Debut Performance Announcement"

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:56.040
The Newcomers' Debut
Performance is almost upon us.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.080
For the five of us...

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.450
...it'll be our first performance together!

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.790
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:20.160
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:27.290
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:35.120
<i>"Purely, delightfully, humorously"</i>

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.620
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:43.160
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:51.410
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:57.700
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:58.750
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:06.200
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.910
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:15.660
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:20.000
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.330
"STARMYU"
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.870
"STARMYU"
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.370
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:41.250
"Act 5"

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.950
It's time, boys!

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.080
We'll start practicing all out for the
debut performance starting from today.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.330
Here, fill this out.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.410
Team Otori's team leader?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:03.120
That's me.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.200
Or not.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.660
Huh? Did you say something, Tsukigami?

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.540
Someone who can't cooperate
with others can't lead this team.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.160
What did you say? I don't want to hear
that from someone with a brother-complex!

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.790
Huh?

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.910
Okay, that's enough.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:24.160
Make sure you decide soon
because you need one for the application.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Now, the piece you'll be performing, "Ayanagi
Showtime," is based on an old musical song.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.950
The story goes something like this:

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.330
There once was a prince who went on a journey.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.080
On his journey, he found a dream and a
sweetheart, but when he became a young man,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:55.290
he had to choose between becoming king,
or continuing on his independent journey.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:03.200
In the end, the prince chose to become
king over his dream and his sweetheart.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.330
"Ayanagi Showtime" is an arrangement
written for the school based on his song

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:13.750
about yearning for his lost freedom
and the sadness he felt.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.910
He gave up on his dream and
his sweetheart for the throne, huh?

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.870
What a silly story.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.540
Yeah, it is silly.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:24.540
I wonder...

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.040
If you become king,
everything goes your way, right?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:35.250
So couldn't he just make his dream
come true and marry his sweetheart?

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.410
Doesn't this song have that excited feeling--

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.250
Hoshitani.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.660
Just how optimistic are you?

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:43.700
Huh?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.790
Just because you become king
doesn't mean everything will go your way.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.200
Really?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.750
The more authority you bear,
the more limitations you'll have.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:56.160
You'll have more things that <i>don't</i> go your way.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.450
Sounds good to me.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.500
We're free.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.120
An excited feeling...

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.120
I worked up a sweat!

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:22.160
The choreography for "Ayanagi Showtime"
isn't hard, but it's hard to stay together.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:36.660
Is that a disguise to
keep fans from chasing you?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:39.200
Good job trying to show us you're popular.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.250
Being jealous because
you're not popular is unseemly.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.540
Shall I introduce you to someone?

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:49.200
No thanks. Unlike you, I'm busy.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.040
Sorry.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.290
There's still some time before dinner.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.370
Wanna stop by somewhere first?

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.450
Welcome!

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:07.750
Um, a double burger meal with
large fries and a small orange juice.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.910
Hey, are you going to be okay
eating that much before dinner?

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.370
No prob!

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.330
I'll have a cheeseburger.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.790
Me too.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.540
Thanks for your order.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.500
Double one, cheese two please!

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.660
What's wrong, Tengenji?

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.790
Wh-What is this?

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.080
This S and M and L?

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.580
Is it a code?

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.290
Tengenji, is it your
first time eating fast food?

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.700
So what if it is?!

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.000
I'm not interested in the food of commoners.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.870
It's his first time...

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.950
He's an endangered species...

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:44.660
"Double Cheeseburger (meal) | Teriyaki Burger"

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.660
How about a teriyaki burger?

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.250
The salty sweet flavors
of the sauce are exquisite.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.080
R-Right, then, I'll have that.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.370
Yum!

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:14.660
Delicious...

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.250
Right?

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:21.870
Later.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.870
Yeah.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.120
Oh yeah, Hoshitani--

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:29.120
I don't mind doing
independent training with you.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:32.750
Your turns aren't perfect yet, right?

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:37.500
I'll go, too. We should practice
"Ayanagi Showtime" together as much as we can

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.660
outside of our lessons at school.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.160
Tengenji... Tsukigami...

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.750
Thanks, everyone!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.330
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.620
One, two, three, fo--

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:00.000
Stop! Let's take a short break.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:06.580
Why do I always mess up at the same place?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.790
Don't worry about it, Hoshitani.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:10.330
The more you worry about it,
the worse it'll get.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.500
Your body's center isn't stable.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:18.330
In order to keep your balance while turning,
you have to strengthen your core.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:22.450
But it takes time to strengthen your core.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.040
I'll try doing more strength training.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.540
I have to do everything I can!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.870
It says classical ballet is good
for strengthening your core...

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.950
It's too late for that.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.000
What's going on?

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.250
Okay, run through it once more.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.620
Yes, sir!

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:18.500
♪ I am going on a journey now ♪

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:21.870
♪ Unfolding the map of old ♪

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:25.450
♪ I am going on a journey now ♪

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.120
♪ Come, let's begin the adventure ♪

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:36.370
♪ I cannot predict what will happen ♪

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:44.540
♪ Who will I meet? My heart flies away on wings ♪

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:51.750
♪ In the fantasy garden with the azure fountain ♪

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:56.160
♪ It blooms only once in a thousand years... ♪

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:01.080
♪ ...this mysterious flower ♪

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:01.910
♪ Go forward! ♪

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:09.120
♪ Continuing the journey far, far away ♪

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:16.250
♪ I will never be afraid of being lonely ♪

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:23.580
♪ Heading for the sun far, far away ♪

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:30.870
♪ A journey to find my true self ♪

00:12:30.870 --> 00:12:32.790
♪ Youth! ♪

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:38.790
♪ It's a brightly shining dream! ♪

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.540
That's Team Hiragi for you.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.540
It's like they know they're the best.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:58.580
Wow, from their gazes to the tips of
their toes, they were completely together.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:07.250
I hate to admit it, but we don't stand a
chance against them as a team right now.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:33.370
Wasn't everyone on Team Hiragi amazing?

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:39.080
At the upcoming debut performance,
half the teams will be cut.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.410
Will we be able to stay?

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.540
What are you saying cowardly things for?

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:47.080
It's not "Will we be able to stay"
but "We're <i>going</i> to stay," you boor!

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:51.160
R-Right... sorry...

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.500
What's wrong, Hoshitani?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.160
I'm going to go back to
school and do more training.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.450
Then, I'll go with you.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:06.500
Sorry, I want to do it by myself today.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.790
Good work.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.910
I heard Team Hiragi's dancing was wonderful.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:25.330
I expect no less from your students.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:32.750
It is my mission to raise capable
people as befits the Ayanagi brand.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:36.790
Oh, that silly Ayanagi brand, huh?

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.450
One of the kids on my team
said something interesting.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:46.660
He said kings should make
their own dreams come true.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:51.080
To protect the throne
he inherited and the kingdom.

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:56.790
Isn't that a dream only
kings are allowed to have?

00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:00.830
It would be best not to
impose your own values on others.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:06.620
I'm not doing that, Your Majesty.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.040
Excuse me.

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:23.040
I just...

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:27.000
...want you to look like you're having more fun.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:56.290
No, that's not right...

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:01.080
What should I do...?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:14.000
That's Team Hiragi for you.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.950
It's like they know they're the best.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:22.160
Wow, from their gazes to the tips of
their toes, they were completely together.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:32.080
I hate to admit it, but we don't stand
a chance against them as a team right now.

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:36.950
At the upcoming debut performance,
half the teams will be cut.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.660
Will we be able to stay?

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.120
Hoshitani?

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:18.950
Wait for me. I'll be done soon.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.120
R-Right...

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.330
You work at a fancy place.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:07.450
Because I can play piano there.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.000
I wanted to do something that
could help with musicals even a little.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:14.200
What's wrong?

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.290
I'm really blessed, huh?

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:22.700
I can do what I love
every day as much as I want.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.750
I'm too blessed...

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.620
I don't have a dad.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:34.080
He died when I was young.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:41.000
Ever since, my mom worked
really hard day and night to raise me.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:47.120
I wanted to make her happy, so I tried
copying the musicals I saw on TV to show her.

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:49.540
I don't think I was very good.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:52.540
But it made her happy.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:58.160
I wanted to make her even happier,
so I became completely absorbed in musicals.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:19:02.540
After a while, I realized how fun it was,

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:06.500
and I wanted to show her a real musical one day.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.040
That is my motivation.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.250
You have yours, too, right?

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:37.290
I read the story of
"Ayanagi Showtime" in a book before.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:41.120
Even the king worried and got depressed.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:44.120
There's no one who just smiles all the time.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.410
Hoshitani!

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:53.120
Nayuki...

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.120
You're still awake?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:58.040
I was worried...

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:01.660
I see. Sorry.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.700
But I'm fine now!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:39.250
You boor, you better not think
you're taking this on all by yourself.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:43.580
We want to worry with you.
Because you're our teammate.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.750
This is just the beginning, right?

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:49.950
You heard them.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:51.620
Everyone...

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:05.410
♪ I'm missing something, but I don't know what ♪

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:11.040
♪ I yearn for the sky I was
looking at that's too far away ♪

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:16.620
♪ What's missing? Look for the answer ♪

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:22.660
♪ We're jumping in again today ♪

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:28.330
♪ The rhythm will not lie ♪

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:33.910
♪ I'll tell you my passionate
feelings through the beat ♪

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:39.580
♪ At times when I'm about to lose heart ♪

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:45.290
♪ I want to give the cheerful guys a good punch ♪

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:50.870
♪ I can't do it alone ♪

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:55.370
♪ Stardust, gather here! ♪

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:01.750
♪ I'm sure, I'm sure tomorrow... ♪

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:07.790
♪ We'll have the most dazzling performance ♪

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:19.120
♪ We'll bring our voices together
to draw people toward us ♪

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:24.750
♪ A message to our adolescence
that has jumped off the sheet music ♪

00:22:24.750 --> 00:22:30.450
♪ So bright it makes our
eyes water, it gives us courage ♪

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:33.250
♪ We're super lucky stars! ♪

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:36.120
♪ Never, ever giving up! ♪

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:44.500
♪ Our hearts become one as we perform ♪

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:49.790
♪ I'm sure, I'm sure tomorrow... ♪

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:55.700
♪ With our ambitions greater than the galaxy ♪

00:22:55.700 --> 00:23:07.660
♪ We'll bring our voices together again and again ♪

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:26.540
Please take this.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:37.330
Looks good to me.

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:42.950
Okay, boys. Why don't we start today's lesson?

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:48.700
"Team Leader Application" Team Name: Team Otori"
"Team Leader | Class: 1-A" "Name: Yuta Hoshitani"

00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:53.000
"Team Leader | Class: 1-A"
"Name: Yuta Hoshitani"

00:23:54.330 --> 00:24:18.750
"Act 6"

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.580
Tsukigami, do you want
to go to a cafe Eigo found?

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.540
It looks like they have that
strawberry <i>au lait</i> that you like.

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:01.540
It's not strawberry <i>au lait,</i>
it's strawberry milk.

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:05.160
Incidentally, five strawberries for 200 cc
of milk is the golden ratio for strawberry milk.

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:07.580
It should be blended for
exactly 45 seconds, please.

00:24:07.580 --> 00:24:09.080
Yup, you're way too serious about this.

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:18.750
"Otori"
"............later."
